<h2>What our cookie policy says about cookie types</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> needed to navigate pages, use secure areas, check out and keep your session secure. These may be used without your consent.</li>
<li><strong>Functional:</strong> remember choices such as language, region, currency and event preferences.</li>
<li><strong>Analytics and performance:</strong> show how visitors use the platform, in aggregated or pseudonymized form.</li>
<li><strong>Advertising and targeting:</strong> deliver more relevant ads, limit how often you see one, and help measure campaigns. Where required by law, these are used only with consent.</li>
</ul>
<p>The policy also explains that cookies can be first-party (set by Seat Outlet) or third-party (set by providers such as analytics, advertising, social and payment partners). Mobile apps may use SDKs that work like cookies.</p>

<h2>How to manage choices under the cookie policy</h2>
<ol>
<li>Use the cookie banner or preferences tool, where available, to accept or reject non-essential categories.</li>
<li>Change browser settings to view, delete or block cookies, or to limit them to first-party only.</li>
<li>On mobile, adjust tracking permissions or reset your advertising ID in your device settings.</li>
<li>Use opt-out tools offered by some advertising partners. These are managed by third parties and may change.</li>
</ol>
<div class="so-callout"><p>Your preferences are stored at the browser or device level, so you may need to set them again if you clear cookies or switch browsers.</p></div>

